1. Scope

"The Work" means everything in this repository that Sorok-Dva authored: the website
and its source code, the Python tools and scripts, the file formats and pipelines,
the documentation, the texts and translations written for Allodex, and the files the
tools produce from the game client, to the extent the author holds any right in them.

This license does not cover:
  a. Allods Online and everything that belongs to its rights holders (Astrum
     Entertainment, MY.GAMES / VK and their licensors): names, trademarks, logos,
     artwork, models, textures, animations, music, sounds, videos, texts and all
     other assets of the game client, including when they are converted, re-encoded
     or re-packed by the tools of this repository (see section 5);
  b. third-party components and content, which keep their own licenses and credits
     (npm and Python dependencies, fonts, the atlas-ao data and texts, community
     images; see the README and the credit files).

2. What you may do

Subject to the conditions below, you may, free of charge, use, copy, modify and
share the Work or parts of it — for example a component, a piece of code, a Python
script or a tool — including in your own projects about Allods Online (WebGL
viewers, fan sites, tools, research), provided those projects are non-commercial.

3. Conditions

  a. Attribution. Any project that uses the Work or a part of it must credit, in a
     place visible to its users (credits page, footer, README, about box):
       "Based on Allodex by Sorok-Dva — https://allodex.eu"
     and keep this license notice with the code you reuse.
  b. Non-commercial use only. You may not sell the Work or any part of it, nor use
     it to earn money, directly or indirectly: no paid access, subscriptions,
     advertising, sponsorships, donations tied to the reused content, paid
     services, sale of files or tools, or inclusion in a paid product.
  c. No substitute site. You may not publish the Work as a whole, or a substantial
     part of the website, as a public website or application that reproduces or
     imitates Allodex — a mirror, a clone, a copy under another name or domain, or
     a site offering essentially the same pages — including a non-commercial one.
     Reusing individual components, pages or tools inside a project that is
     clearly your own is allowed under section 2.
  d. No confusion. You may not present your project as Allodex, as endorsed by
     Allodex or its author, or use the Allodex name or logo other than to give the
     credit above.
  e. Changes. If you share a modified version of a part of the Work, state that you
     changed it.

Any use outside these terms requires the prior written permission of the author.

4. Termination

Any breach of these terms ends your rights under this license automatically. They
are restored if you stop the breach within 30 days after being notified of it for
the first time.

5. Game content

The author cannot and does not grant any right on the content of Allods Online. The
extraction tools are shared for study, preservation and fan projects. Whoever reuses
game content, raw or converted, does so under their own responsibility and must
respect the rights and terms of its owners.

6. No warranty

The Work is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The author is not
liable for any damage arising from its use.

